    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but isn't the idea that these countries \"chose\" to join NATO just a way for the West to deflect responsibility for how they actually handled the situation? it feels like the \"sovereignty\" argument is just a cover for expansionism.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You raise a valid point that some critics argue this narrative shifts the blame from historical Russian overreach to the hesitation of neighboring states. By framing the alliance as a \"choice,\" supporters emphasize democratic self-determination and the security preferences of the participating nations. Ultimately, while the 1957 Paris Treaty affirmed EU non-oversight on \"enlargement policy,\" the debate often centers on whether inclusion in the alliance truly promoted stability or inadvertently led to the very conflict the West sought to avoid.",
